title The ball at your own goal
intro You have the ball in front of your own goal.
flip vertical

setup
  lineup 7v7
  player B-CB at 14, 34
  player R-LF at 28, 34
  player R-RF at 22, 48
  ball with B-CB

step
  caption You are the defender in blue. Watch what happens.
  label B-CB You
  draw penalty-area left

step
  caption Red closes you down, right in front of your own goal.
  R-LF to 17, 34
  R-RF to 18, 46
  arrow from R-LF to B-CB
  arrow from R-RF to 16, 42
  draw penalty-area left
  duration 1000

question
  prompt What is the best move?
  answer Kick it wide, toward the sideline
  wrong Pass it across in front of your goal
  wrong Dribble through the middle
  wrong Stand on the ball and wait
  correct Send it wide.
  why A pass across your own goal is the riskiest ball in soccer. If Red cuts it out, they shoot straight away.

question
  prompt Nobody is free. Where should it go?
  answer High and wide, away from the middle
  wrong Back into the middle
  wrong Straight into your goalie's hands
  wrong Over your own goal line
  correct High and wide.
  why When you are stuck, get the ball away from your goal. Your team can chase it and win it back up the field.
